  "conformance_claims": [
    "All core object schemas and status enums are machine-readable and validated.",
    "Content hashes use RFC 8785 canonicalization followed by SHA-256 with schema version included.",
    "Four statuses are stored and validated independently; collapsed status is a conformance failure.",
    "Frozen objects are append-only; post-freeze mutation is rejected with a machine-readable reason code.",
    "Opportunity classification honors 0 <= delta_noop < delta_positive <= 1 and Pi_cert/Pi_auth_pub separation.",
    "Search and certification seed isolation is enforced; leakage and certification optimization are negative fixtures.",
    "Replay, terminal verdicts, primary assignment and splits are deterministic and golden-fixture-bound.",
    "Public/private Episode records are separated; gold_actions is enforced empty.",
    "The e2e fixture fixes expected hashes, labels, assignment, split, replay digest and terminal verdict.",
    "The package does not scan real backends or construct real Episodes; only embedded synthetic fixture processes are consumed."
  ],
  "test_command": "python3 tests/run_all.py",
  "known_limitations": [
    "Golden hashes were produced by this reference implementation and frozen in the package; canonicalization is independently anchored to RFC 8785 vectors.",
    "Semantic entailment (Query/Contract) is represented by frozen two-annotator verdicts and structural consistency checks, not by automated NLU.",
    "The tiny corpus in the e2e fixture cannot meet the real admission frequency gates; admission fields are synthetic fixture values, not benchmark claims.",
    "Physical processes in fixtures are embedded synthetic traces, not real backend scans.",
    "RFC 8785 number formatting is frozen by RFC examples plus explicit ECMAScript 1e-6 and 1e21 boundary fixtures.",
    "The content hash excludes the mutable statuses lifecycle block so freeze/release transitions never change a version's content address; statuses are validated independently.",
    "The machine-readable inference matrix extends the prose may_support column of spec section 2.1 with directly-stated semantic fields; cannot_establish_alone is binding and faithful."
  ],
  "hash_algorithm": "SHA-256(raw artifact bytes); RFC 8785 for release tuple",
